<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan reinvites bids for 5,000-T rice export.</title>
<headline>Pakistan reinvites bids for 5,000-T rice export.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Rice Export Corporation of Pakistan (RECP) on Monday invited new bids for the sale and export of 5,000 tonnes of basmati variety Pak-7 1996/97 (July-June) rice containing seven percent broken.</p>
<p>An RECP official said bids, to be submitted by June 16, had been reinvited after the corporation scrapped an earlier tender for the sale and export of the same quantity of basmati.</p>
<p>He said the corporation felt the three bids opened on May 26 were too low at $436 per tonne FOB, $435.10 and $425.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
